      "gap": "Nearly all of Milton's treatment is reconstructed, but two of Milton's own conclusions/qualifications are absent. (1) Milton p. 8 draws from the two-sentence Didaskalikos treatment the conclusion that the Platonists lacked any serious interest in induction; lines 404-413 report only the brevity and content, not that inference. (2) Milton p. 29 states that there is no further discussion of induction in the works Descartes published; lines 1168-1176 and 1247-1252 say only that induction plays no significant role in the mature philosophy and report the Regulae's 1701 printing, which is a different claim.",
